  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (176 tests, 0 failed), including the new ones.\n\n- **Store (`src/store.js`):** I added `reserve`, `getAvailable`, `confirm` and `release`, and `removeItem` now checks against available stock instead of physical stock. All time checks use the store's `clock`. `confirm` also returns `{sku, qty}`, which the API uses for its response.\n- **API (`src/api.js`):** `GET /stock/:sku` now also returns `available`, and I added the three reservation routes with the status codes you listed.\n- **Tests (`test/reservations.test.js`):** these cover the exact expiry boundary, each error case, `release` called twice or with an unknown id, `removeItem` against reserved stock, and each new route's statuses.\n- **Not validated:** `ttlMs` isn't checked, since you didn't specify rules for it. A missing or non-numeric value makes the reservation expire immediately.\n- **Memory growth:** expired reservations stay in memory until someone confirms or releases them, because `confirm` has to tell \"expired\" apart from \"not found\".\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
